> Personally? I wouldn't move a square until I had an amulet of lifesaving
> on. If you die without one, you will kick yourself very hard, and if you
> don't die, you will have won the game, so it was obviously a good enough
> choice. Improving basics like MR, reflection, and AC before wishing
> for lifesaving is reasonable but, if you don't intend to to wish for
> artifacts, I can't think of anything with a better potential return this
> early in the game.
>
> Even if you did intend to wish for artifacts, I would be torn between
> AoLS and Gauntlets of Defense (which I would likely have picked up
> instead of the speed boots, but your choices were fine).

Yep, Water Walking boots might be better than speed in Slash'em, but maybe  
not in the early game...

For the middle/late game, some way of preventing draining (wands !) is  
needed. If you're lawfull, Excalibur can do the trick, otherwise amulet or  
DDSM, but that's not for the early game.

Yes, I agree that AoLS might be a pretty good choice in the early game  
after getting AC, speed, MR and reflection...

If you're a doppelgagner, you might prefer an amulet of unchanging  
(Crystal golems rule).

If you're wishing for artefact, the super-BoH can be nice... Anyway, a  
regular BoH can also help but probably after AoLS since you can always  
stash stuff (and not lives).

If you're a Vampire, you probably want something to keep that hunger at  
bay. Ring of SD is nice but the medecine bag is probably better (feeds you  
*and* keeps your level low).

Of course, a couple of scrolls of genocide can always help you out of some  
thight spots...

